          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>The Kaggle dataset is synthetic, so findings are illustrative and should be validated with real data before acting.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>It has no customer ID, country or return cost, which limits the search for stronger drivers.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Collect richer, real data:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'> customer ID (repeat buyers and serial returners), country (return behavior by market) and return cost.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Focus on a brand and country:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'> analyze purchases and returns of a specific brand in a specific market (e.g. Mango in Portugal), using customer-level analysis and multi-variable models.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'>Pilot the recommendations:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='10'> test size information, loyalty rules and return policy on a small group, and track return rate and cost per return.</run>
          </formatted-text>
